  "scientific_assessment": {
    "coarse_phase_field_status": "In PK_HOLE_COARSE_JOB1.odb (518.2 MB, SHA-256: 834b9bb0...), the UEL-UMAT formulation used f42_mixed_uel.for, where Layer 3 visualizer UMAT explicitly sets STRESS(I) = 0.D0 with dummy stiffness DDSDDE(I,I) = 1.D-11. Consequently, Cauchy stress S and native MISESERI error indicators are identically zero across all 389 increments. PK_HOLE_COARSE_JOB1.odb alone CANNOT serve as a native MISESERI donor without a companion stress-recovery operation. At Step-2 Peak (Frame 167, t = 0.3277, uy = 0.00729 mm, F_max = 0.7310 kN), damage localization reaches d_max = 0.5798. Independent element-adjacency analysis confirms that the 48 damaged elements (d >= 0.10) form 3 edge-connected components: a primary crack lobe of 37 elements originating 9.5 um from the notch tip and terminating 7.69 um (1.02 l0) from the hole boundary; a secondary crack lobe of 10 elements on the opposite hole flank (within 7.85 um of hole boundary); and 1 boundary constraint element. Damage connectivity does not span the full ligament: a physical gap of 7.69 um remains before hole penetration.",
    "falsifiable_scientific_hypothesis": "HYPOTHESIS F1728-H2-CASE2: Native Abaqus UNIFORM_ERROR remeshing driven by linear-elastic pre-analysis (Step-1, Donor 1) will produce a mesh highly refined at the notch root (h <= l0/2) but coarse across the uncracked oblique ligament into the hole flank (h > l0/2). Conversely, driving adaptive remeshing from an authentic phase-field donor state at peak load requires companion degraded Cauchy stress recovery to generate nonzero stress jumps across the primary crack lobe.",
    "preanalysis_behavior": "Under linear-elastic pre-analysis (Step-1, u2 = 0.0050 mm, PK_HOLE_METHOD_A_PREANALYSIS.odb), MISESERI strongly concentrates at the singular notch tip (max = 1430.27 MPa, mean in tip core = 385.55 MPa, yielding a maximum-to-bulk contrast of 95.11x and core-mean-to-bulk contrast of 25.64x vs bulk mean 15.04 MPa). At the hole flank boundary, mean error is 162.63 MPa (10.81x bulk), and along the notch-to-hole ligament mean error is 193.96 MPa. Because the notch tip singularity is an order of magnitude higher than the ligament error, native Abaqus UNIFORM_ERROR remeshing driven by linear-elastic pre-analysis will refine the notch tip but starve the uncracked oblique ligament connecting the crack tip to the hole, exactly as observed in Case 1.",
    "recommended_next_execution_dependency": "1. Candidate Donor 1 (PK_HOLE_METHOD_A_PREANALYSIS.odb) is the ONLY currently qualified donor possessing a native, nonzero MISESERI field (max = 1430.27 MPa). It is ready for baseline technical parity remeshing.\n2. To utilize Step-2 Peak damage information, a companion stress-recovery operation must be independently qualified to compute the degraded Cauchy stress field before native remeshing can be executed."
